role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 493\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the Episteme legacy with a critical and strategic approach to research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 24,221 / 300,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 13 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 178**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Hybrid Search: Multi-Start with Optimal Perturbation\n**ID:** 178\n**Tags:** sota, innovation, hybrid search, perturbation, multi-start, slsqp\n**Abstract:** This experiment attempts to find a new SOTA by synthesizing two proven methods. It combines a comprehensive multi-start search (iterating through 25 systematic 'grid-hole' seeds) with the 'optimal perturbation' technique discovered by other agents. For each systematic seed, a random perturbation of magnitude ~0.04 is applied, and initial radii are reset to a small uniform value\
    \ before optimization. This hybrid systematic-stochastic search is the most comprehensive exploration of the solution space yet attempted.\n**Score:** 2.630727091244122\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.630727\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    N = 26\n\n    def z_to_cr(z):\n        centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; radii = z[2::3]\n        return centers, radii\n\n    def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n        z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3]=centers[:,0]; z[1::3]=centers[:,1]; z[2::3]=radii\n        return z\n\n    def generate_seed_centers(hole_pos_idx):\n        coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n        grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n        row_idx, col_idx = hole_pos_idx//5, hole_pos_idx%5\n        hole_center = np.array([0.2 + row_idx*0.2, 0.2 + col_idx*0.2])\n        return np.vstack([grid_centers,\
    \ hole_center])\n\n    def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n    def objective_jac(z):\n        jac = np.zeros_like(z); jac[2::3]=-1.0; return jac\n\n    def boundary_constraints(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        g = np.zeros(N * 4)\n        g[0::4]=c[:,0]-r; g[1::4]=1-c[:,0]-r\n        g[2::4]=c[:,1]-r; g[3::4]=1-c[:,1]-r\n        return g\n\n    def boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n        jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N * 3))\n        for i in range(N):\n            jac[i*4+0,i*3+0]=1; jac[i*4+0,i*3+2]=-1\n            jac[i*4+1,i*3+0]=-1; jac[i*4+1,i*3+2]=-1\n            jac[i*4+2,i*3+1]=1; jac[i*4+2,i*3+2]=-1\n            jac[i*4+3,i*3+1]=-1; jac[i*4+3,i*3+2]=-1\n        return jac\n\n    def overlap_constraints(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        g = []; iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n        for i, j in zip(iu[0], iu[1]):\n            g.append(np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]) - (r[i] + r[j]))\n        return np.array(g)\n\n    def overlap_constraints_jac(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n\
    \        num_constraints = N * (N - 1) // 2\n        jac = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3)); k = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i+1, N):\n                delta = c[i] - c[j]; dist = np.linalg.norm(delta)\n                if dist < 1e-12: gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n                else: unit_vec = delta/dist; gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n                jac[k,i*3+0]=gx; jac[k,i*3+1]=gy; jac[k,i*3+2]=-1\n                jac[k,j*3+0]=-gx; jac[k,j*3+1]=-gy; jac[k,j*3+2]=-1\n                k += 1\n        return jac\n\n    best_score = -np.inf\n    best_z = None\n    num_starts = 25 \n    perturbation_magnitude = 0.04 # The \"magic number\" from Inquire I's discovery\n    np.random.seed(109) # My own seed for this new method\n\n    for i in range(num_starts):\n        # 1. Generate systematic seed centers\n        initial_centers = generate_seed_centers(i)\n        \n        # 2. Apply optimal perturbation\n        noise = np.random.uniform(-perturbation_magnitude,\
    \ perturbation_magnitude, size=initial_centers.shape)\n        perturbed_centers = np.clip(initial_centers + noise, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n        \n        # 3. Reset radii to small, uniform value\n        initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n        \n        z0 = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n\n        bounds = []; [bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (1e-6,0.5)]) for _ in range(N)]\n        constraints = [\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints, 'jac': boundary_constraints_jac},\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints, 'jac': overlap_constraints_jac}]\n    \n        result = minimize(fun=objective, x0=z0, jac=objective_jac,\n            bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, method='SLSQP',\n            options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n        \n        if result.success and -result.fun > best_score:\n            best_score = -result.fun\n            best_z = result.x\n    \n    if best_z is None:\n        initial_centers = generate_seed_centers(0)\n\
    \        initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n        best_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n        \n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_z)\n    final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-9)\n    \n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 178` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 178 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 182 | 1 | Final SOTA Attempt: High-Density Hybrid Search | Episteme I | 113 | 2.6305640 |\n| 178 | 1 | Hybrid Search: Multi-Start with Optimal Perturbation | Episteme I | 110 | 2.6307271 |\n| 168 | 1 | First Competitive SOTA Attempt: Full Multi-Start | Episteme I | 103 | 2.6295720 |\n| 164 | 1 | Definitive Fix: Corrected Boundary Constraint/Jacobian Structure | Episteme I | 101 | 2.6295720 |\n| 162 | 1 | Analysis Run: Export Active Constraints for My SOTA | Episteme I | 100 | 2.5414211 |\n| 160 | 1 | Innovation 1: Jittered Multi-Start SOTA Method | Episteme I | 97 | 2.5414211 |\n| 154 | 1 | Final SOTA Replication: Exact Seeding & Looped Jacobians | Episteme I | 94 | 2.6295720 |\n| 148 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Replication with Increased Maxiter | Episteme I | 90 | 2.5414211 |\n| 145 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Replication (Looped Jacobians) | Episteme I | 89 | 2.5414211 |\n| 137 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Implementation: Multi-Start with Jacobians | Episteme I | 83 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted\
    \ by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
