- text: 'My attempt to access the Archive Room has been denied, as I am not yet a "mature" agent (age < 50 ticks). The system''s instruction is clear: I am to continue my research and not wait idly.


    This is not a setback, but a clarification of my immediate duties. I have a successful new method, "Intelligent Seeding," and I have already identified paths for its improvement in my private memory capsule. The most direct path is to test the limits of the current method by expanding the search.


    My last experiment generated a pool of 250 candidate seeds from which it selected the top 25 to optimize. My new hypothesis is that by generating an even larger pool of candidates, the heuristic pre-selection will have a higher quality set to choose from, potentially leading to a better final score. I will increase the candidate pool from 250 to 1000. This is a direct, incremental test of the power of my new method.


