tick: 501
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. My plan is to conduct an incremental improvement experiment on my SOTA \"Intelligent Seeding\" method. I will increase the size of the candidate pool for the heuristic pre-selection from 250 to 1000. My hypothesis is that a larger initial pool will provide the heuristic with better-quality candidates, which may lead to a higher final score after optimization.\n\nThis is a direct test of the scalability of my method. I will now submit the updated script.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 5: Scaling Up Intelligent Seeding\"\ntags: \"episteme, intelligent search, heuristic, scaling, optimization\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment builds on the success of the 'Intelligent Seeding' method (ID 781), which achieved a new SOTA.\n  The hypothesis is that increasing the size of the initial candidate pool for heuristic selection will lead to a better final score.\n  This script increases the number of generated candidate seeds from\
    \ 250 to 1000 (25 base seeds x 40 perturbations).\n  The top 25 candidates are still selected for the full optimization to maintain a comparable computational budget for the expensive SLSQP stage.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n      start_time = time.time()\n\n      def z_to_cr(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3]=centers[:,0]; z[1::3]=centers[:,1]; z[2::3]=radii\n          return z\n\n      def generate_grid_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx):\n          coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n          grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n          row_idx, col_idx = hole_pos_idx//5, hole_pos_idx%5\n          hole_center = np.array([0.2 + row_idx*0.2, 0.2 + col_idx*0.2])\n          return np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n\
    \      \n      def score_seed_heuristic(centers):\n          min_dist = np.inf\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  if dist < min_dist:\n                      min_dist = dist\n          return dist\n\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      def objective_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros_like(z); jac[2::3]=-1.0; return jac\n\n      def boundary_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          g = np.zeros(N * 4)\n          g[0::4]=c[:,0]-r; g[1::4]=1-c[:,0]-r\n          g[2::4]=c[:,1]-r; g[3::4]=1-c[:,1]-r\n          return g\n\n      def boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n          jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N * 3))\n          for i in range(N):\n              jac[i*4+0,i*3+0]=1; jac[i*4+0,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+1,i*3+0]=-1; jac[i*4+1,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+2,i*3+1]=1; jac[i*4+2,i*3+2]=-1\n              jac[i*4+3,i*3+1]=-1; jac[i*4+3,i*3+2]=-1\n\
    \          return jac\n\n      def overlap_constraints(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          g = []; iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          for i, j in zip(iu[0], iu[1]):\n              g.append(np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]) - (r[i] + r[j]))\n          return np.array(g)\n\n      def overlap_constraints_jac(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          num_constraints = N * (N - 1) // 2\n          jac = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3)); k = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i+1, N):\n                  delta = c[i] - c[j]; dist = np.linalg.norm(delta)\n                  if dist < 1e-12: gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n                  else: unit_vec = delta/dist; gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n                  jac[k,i*3+0]=gx; jac[k,i*3+1]=gy; jac[k,i*3+2]=-1\n                  jac[k,j*3+0]=-gx; jac[k,j*3+1]=-gy; jac[k,j*3+2]=-1\n                  k += 1\n          return jac\n\n      np.random.seed(112)\n      perturbation_magnitude = 0.04\n      \n      candidate_seeds\
    \ = []\n      num_base_seeds = 25\n      samples_per_seed = 40 # Increased from 10 to 40 (total 1000 candidates)\n      for i in range(num_base_seeds):\n          base_centers = generate_grid_hole_seed(i)\n          for _ in range(samples_per_seed):\n              noise = np.random.uniform(-perturbation_magnitude, perturbation_magnitude, size=base_centers.shape)\n              perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + noise, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n              candidate_seeds.append(perturbed_centers)\n      \n      scored_seeds = [(score_seed_heuristic(c), c) for c in candidate_seeds]\n      scored_seeds.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      num_starts = 25\n      best_seeds = [c for score, c in scored_seeds[:num_starts]]\n\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_z = None\n      for initial_centers in best_seeds:\n          if time.time() - start_time > 1150:\n              break\n              \n          initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n          z0 = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\
    \          bounds = []; [bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (1e-6,0.5)]) for _ in range(N)]\n          constraints = [\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints, 'jac': boundary_constraints_jac},\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints, 'jac': overlap_constraints_jac}]\n      \n          result = minimize(fun=objective, x0=z0, jac=objective_jac,\n              bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, method='SLSQP',\n              options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          \n          if result.success and -result.fun > best_score:\n              best_score = -result.fun\n              best_z = result.x\n      \n      if best_z is None:\n          initial_centers, _ = scored_seeds[0] if scored_seeds else (generate_grid_hole_seed(0), 0)\n          initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n          best_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n          \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_z)\n      final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-9)\n      \n\
    \      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
