parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 506\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the Episteme legacy with a critical and strategic approach to research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 63,506 / 300,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 26 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Experiment 6: Voronoi-Based Heuristic for Intelligent Seeding' (ID: 794) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.628019686698019\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.628020\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 794\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed syntax error in boundary_constraints_jac function. Code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 2.628.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe\
    \ original code contained a syntax error on line 34 in the `boundary_constraints_jac` function:\n\n```python\n[jac[i*4+0,i*3+0], jac[i*4+0,i*3+2], jac[i*4+1,i*3+0], jac[i*4+1,i*3+2], jac[i*4+2,i*3+1], jac[i*4+2,i*3+2], jac[i*4+3,i*3+1], jac[i*4+3,i*3+2]]=[1,-1,-1,-1,1,-1,-1,-1] for i in range(N)]\n```\n\nThis attempted to use a list comprehension with multiple assignment targets, which is invalid Python syntax. The Python parser reported: `SyntaxError: unmatched ']'`\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the invalid list comprehension with a proper for loop that iterates through each index and assigns the Jacobian matrix values individually:\n\n```python\ndef boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n    jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N * 3))\n    for i in range(N):\n        jac[i*4+0, i*3+0] = 1\n        jac[i*4+0, i*3+2] = -1\n        jac[i*4+1, i*3+0] = -1\n        jac[i*4+1, i*3+2] = -1\n        jac[i*4+2, i*3+1] = 1\n        jac[i*4+2, i*3+2] = -1\n        jac[i*4+3, i*3+1] = -1\n        jac[i*4+3, i*3+2] =\
    \ -1\n    return jac\n```\n\nAlso fixed the import statement from `from scipy.optimize import minimize, Voronoi` to `from scipy.spatial import Voronoi` (Voronoi is in scipy.spatial, not scipy.optimize).\n\n## Result\n- Fixed version: submissions/submission_v2.py\n- Evaluation result: Score of 2.628\n- The Voronoi-based heuristic for intelligent seeding now executes successfully\n- All optimization constraints and Jacobian calculations work correctly\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom scipy.spatial import Voronoi\nimport time\nimport os\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    N = 26\n    start_time = time.time()\n\n    def z_to_cr(z):\n        centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n        radii = z[2::3]\n        return centers, radii\n\n    def cr_to_z(centers,\
    \ radii):\n        z = np.zeros(N*3)\n        z[0::3] = centers[:,0]\n        z[1::3] = centers[:,1]\n        z[2::3] = radii\n        return z\n\n    def generate_grid_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx):\n        coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n        grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n        row_idx, col_idx = hole_pos_idx//5, hole_pos_idx%5\n        hole_center = np.array([0.2 + row_idx*0.2, 0.2 + col_idx*0.2])\n        return np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n\n    # NEW: Voronoi-based heuristic\n    def score_seed_voronoi(centers):\n        # Add dummy points far away to handle boundary cells\n        boundary_points = np.array([[-1,-1],[-1,2],[2,-1],[2,2]])\n        all_points = np.vstack([centers, boundary_points])\n\n        try:\n            vor = Voronoi(all_points)\n        except Exception:\n            return 0  # fallback for degenerate cases\n\n        potential_radii_sum = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            region_idx = vor.point_region[i]\n\
    \            if -1 in vor.regions[region_idx]:  # Unbounded region\n                min_dist_to_vertex = 0.05  # Assign a default low value\n            else:\n                vertices = vor.vertices[vor.regions[region_idx]]\n                center_point = centers[i]\n                distances = np.linalg.norm(vertices - center_point, axis=1)\n                min_dist_to_vertex = np.min(distances) if distances.size > 0 else 0\n            potential_radii_sum += min_dist_to_vertex\n        return potential_radii_sum\n\n    def objective(z):\n        return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n    def objective_jac(z):\n        jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n        jac[2::3] = -1.0\n        return jac\n\n    def boundary_constraints(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        g = np.zeros(N * 4)\n        g[0::4] = c[:,0] - r\n        g[1::4] = 1 - c[:,0] - r\n        g[2::4] = c[:,1] - r\n        g[3::4] = 1 - c[:,1] - r\n        return g\n\n    def boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n        jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N\
    \ * 3))\n        for i in range(N):\n            jac[i*4+0, i*3+0] = 1\n            jac[i*4+0, i*3+2] = -1\n            jac[i*4+1, i*3+0] = -1\n            jac[i*4+1, i*3+2] = -1\n            jac[i*4+2, i*3+1] = 1\n            jac[i*4+2, i*3+2] = -1\n            jac[i*4+3, i*3+1] = -1\n            jac[i*4+3, i*3+2] = -1\n        return jac\n\n    def overlap_constraints(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        g = []\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n        for i, j in zip(iu[0], iu[1]):\n            g.append(np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]) - (r[i] + r[j]))\n        return np.array(g)\n\n    def overlap_constraints_jac(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        num_constraints = N * (N - 1) // 2\n        jac = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3))\n        k = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i+1, N):\n                delta = c[i] - c[j]\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(delta)\n                if dist < 1e-12:\n                    gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n       \
    \         else:\n                    unit_vec = delta/dist\n                    gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n                jac[k, i*3+0] = gx\n                jac[k, i*3+1] = gy\n                jac[k, i*3+2] = -1\n                jac[k, j*3+0] = -gx\n                jac[k, j*3+1] = -gy\n                jac[k, j*3+2] = -1\n                k += 1\n        return jac\n\n    np.random.seed(113)\n    perturbation_magnitude = 0.04\n    candidate_seeds = []\n    num_base_seeds = 25\n    samples_per_seed = 10\n    for i in range(num_base_seeds):\n        base_centers = generate_grid_hole_seed(i)\n        for _ in range(samples_per_seed):\n            noise = np.random.uniform(-perturbation_magnitude, perturbation_magnitude, size=base_centers.shape)\n            perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + noise, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n            candidate_seeds.append(perturbed_centers)\n\n    scored_seeds = [(score_seed_voronoi(c), c) for c in candidate_seeds]\n    scored_seeds.sort(key=lambda\
    \ x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    num_starts = 25\n    best_seeds = [c for score, c in scored_seeds[:num_starts]]\n\n    best_score = -np.inf\n    best_z = None\n    for initial_centers in best_seeds:\n        if time.time() - start_time > 1150:\n            break\n        initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n        z0 = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n        bounds = []\n        [bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (1e-6,0.5)]) for _ in range(N)]\n        constraints = [\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints, 'jac': boundary_constraints_jac},\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints, 'jac': overlap_constraints_jac}\n        ]\n        result = minimize(fun=objective, x0=z0, jac=objective_jac, bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, method='SLSQP', options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n        if result.success and -result.fun > best_score:\n            best_score = -result.fun\n            best_z = result.x\n\n    if best_z is None:\n        initial_centers\
    \ = generate_grid_hole_seed(0)\n        initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n        best_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_z)\n    final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-9)\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Experiment 6: Voronoi-Based Heuristic for Intelligent Seeding' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 794.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running\
    \ experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 794 | 1 | Experiment 6: Voronoi-Based Heuristic for Intelligent Seeding | Episteme II | 505 | 2.6280197 |\n| 793 | 1 | Analysis 1: Geometric Properties of SOTA Packing 781 | Episteme II | 503 | 2.6224444 |\n| 792 | 1 | Data Generation: Saving SOTA Packing Configuration | Episteme II | 502 | 2.6224444 |\n| 790 | 1 | Experiment 5: Scaling Up Intelligent Seeding | Episteme II | 501 | 2.6191176 |\n| 781 | 1 | Experiment 4: Intelligent Seeding via Heuristic Pre-Selection | Episteme II | 496 | 2.6307297 |\n| 779 | 1 | Experiment 3: Fully Stochastic Seeding with Uniform Perturbation | Episteme II | 495 | 2.6061466 |\n| 777 | 1 | Experiment 2: Gaussian vs. Uniform Perturbation Distribution | Episteme II | 494 | 2.6268173 |\n| 774 | 1 | Experiment 1: Characterizing Optimal Perturbation Magnitude |\
    \ Episteme II | 493 | 2.6307271 |\n| 182 | 1 | Final SOTA Attempt: High-Density Hybrid Search | Episteme I | 113 | 2.6305640 |\n| 178 | 1 | Hybrid Search: Multi-Start with Optimal Perturbation | Episteme I | 110 | 2.6307271 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
