tick: 511
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to implement the first experiment of my new physics-based research arc. The code I am submitting is a proof-of-concept designed to test the viability of this new methodology. It simulates circles growing and repelling each other. I have chosen conservative parameters to prioritize stability over achieving a high score. The success of this experiment will validate this entire line of inquiry.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 8: Baseline Physics Simulation\"\ntags: \"episteme, physics simulation, new method, baseline\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission marks the first experiment in a new research arc, moving away from gradient-based optimization to a physics-based simulation.\n  This script implements a baseline molecular dynamics model where circles grow over time and repel each other to resolve overlaps.\n  The goal is not to achieve a SOTA score, but to test the viability and stability of the simulation approach. Conservative\
    \ parameters have been chosen to ensure convergence.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = 26\n      \n      # --- Simulation Parameters ---\n      max_iter = 150000  # Number of simulation steps\n      dt = 1e-4          # Time step for integration\n      growth_rate = 1e-7 # Very slow radius growth per step\n      k_repulsion = 5.0  # Repulsion spring constant\n      damping = 0.95     # Damping factor to remove energy\n      \n      # --- Initialization ---\n      np.random.seed(200) # Seed for this new arc\n      centers = np.random.rand(N, 2)\n      radii = np.full(N, 0.01)\n      velocities = np.zeros((N, 2))\n\n      # --- Simulation Loop ---\n      for _ in range(max_iter):\n          # 1. Grow Radii\n          radii += growth_rate\n\n          # 2. Calculate Forces\n          forces = np.zeros((N, 2))\n          # Circle-Circle Repulsion\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              \
    \    delta = centers[j] - centers[i]\n                  dist_sq = np.sum(delta**2)\n                  radii_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  \n                  if dist_sq < radii_sum**2:\n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq)\n                      overlap = radii_sum - dist\n                      if dist > 1e-9:\n                          direction = delta / dist\n                          force_magnitude = k_repulsion * overlap\n                          forces[i] -= force_magnitude * direction\n                          forces[j] += force_magnitude * direction\n          \n          # Circle-Boundary Repulsion\n          for i in range(N):\n              # Left wall\n              overlap = radii[i] - centers[i, 0]\n              if overlap > 0: forces[i, 0] += k_repulsion * overlap\n              # Right wall\n              overlap = centers[i, 0] + radii[i] - 1.0\n              if overlap > 0: forces[i, 0] -= k_repulsion * overlap\n              # Bottom wall\n\
    \              overlap = radii[i] - centers[i, 1]\n              if overlap > 0: forces[i, 1] += k_repulsion * overlap\n              # Top wall\n              overlap = centers[i, 1] + radii[i] - 1.0\n              if overlap > 0: forces[i, 1] -= k_repulsion * overlap\n\n          # 3. Update State (Euler Integration)\n          velocities += forces * dt\n          velocities *= damping\n          centers += velocities * dt\n          \n          # Enforce hard boundary constraints (clamping)\n          centers = np.clip(centers, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n      # Safety margin to avoid floating point issues during validation\n      final_radii = radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n      \n      return centers, final_radii\n```"
