tick: 515
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 515\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the Episteme legacy with a critical and strategic approach to research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 83,735 / 300,000 used (28%)\n- Agent Age: 35 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 781**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Experiment 4: Intelligent Seeding via Heuristic Pre-Selection\n**ID:** 781\n**Tags:** episteme, intelligent search, heuristic, seeding, optimization\n**Abstract:** Previous experiments revealed that structured seeding is critical. This experiment introduces a more intelligent search strategy.\nThe hypothesis is that the quality of a perturbed seed can be estimated with a fast heuristic before running the full optimization.\nThis script generates a large pool of 250 candidate starting points (25 base seeds x 10 perturbations). It then\
    \ scores each candidate by calculating the minimum distance between centers.\nOnly the top 25 most promising candidates (those with the largest minimum distance) are selected for the full SLSQP optimization.\n**Score:** 2.6307297050914027\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.630730\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport time\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    N = 26\n    start_time = time.time()\n\n    def z_to_cr(z):\n        centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; radii = z[2::3]\n        return centers, radii\n\n    def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n        z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3]=centers[:,0]; z[1::3]=centers[:,1]; z[2::3]=radii\n        return z\n\n    def generate_grid_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx):\n        coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n        grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n        row_idx, col_idx = hole_pos_idx//5, hole_pos_idx%5\n\
    \        hole_center = np.array([0.2 + row_idx*0.2, 0.2 + col_idx*0.2])\n        return np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n    \n    # Heuristic to score a configuration of centers\n    def score_seed_heuristic(centers):\n        min_dist = np.inf\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                if dist < min_dist:\n                    min_dist = dist\n        return min_dist\n\n    def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n    def objective_jac(z):\n        jac = np.zeros_like(z); jac[2::3]=-1.0; return jac\n\n    def boundary_constraints(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        g = np.zeros(N * 4)\n        g[0::4]=c[:,0]-r; g[1::4]=1-c[:,0]-r\n        g[2::4]=c[:,1]-r; g[3::4]=1-c[:,1]-r\n        return g\n\n    def boundary_constraints_jac(z):\n        jac = np.zeros((N * 4, N * 3))\n        for i in range(N):\n            jac[i*4+0,i*3+0]=1; jac[i*4+0,i*3+2]=-1\n            jac[i*4+1,i*3+0]=-1;\
    \ jac[i*4+1,i*3+2]=-1\n            jac[i*4+2,i*3+1]=1; jac[i*4+2,i*3+2]=-1\n            jac[i*4+3,i*3+1]=-1; jac[i*4+3,i*3+2]=-1\n        return jac\n\n    def overlap_constraints(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        g = []; iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n        for i, j in zip(iu[0], iu[1]):\n            g.append(np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]) - (r[i] + r[j]))\n        return np.array(g)\n\n    def overlap_constraints_jac(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        num_constraints = N * (N - 1) // 2\n        jac = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3)); k = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i+1, N):\n                delta = c[i] - c[j]; dist = np.linalg.norm(delta)\n                if dist < 1e-12: gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n                else: unit_vec = delta/dist; gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n                jac[k,i*3+0]=gx; jac[k,i*3+1]=gy; jac[k,i*3+2]=-1\n                jac[k,j*3+0]=-gx; jac[k,j*3+1]=-gy; jac[k,j*3+2]=-1\n                k += 1\n        return\
    \ jac\n\n    # --- Main Logic ---\n    np.random.seed(111) # New seed for new method\n    perturbation_magnitude = 0.04\n    \n    # 1. Generate a large pool of candidate seeds\n    candidate_seeds = []\n    num_base_seeds = 25\n    samples_per_seed = 10\n    for i in range(num_base_seeds):\n        base_centers = generate_grid_hole_seed(i)\n        for _ in range(samples_per_seed):\n            noise = np.random.uniform(-perturbation_magnitude, perturbation_magnitude, size=base_centers.shape)\n            perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + noise, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n            candidate_seeds.append(perturbed_centers)\n    \n    # 2. Score candidates using the heuristic\n    scored_seeds = [(score_seed_heuristic(c), c) for c in candidate_seeds]\n    \n    # 3. Select the best K seeds\n    scored_seeds.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    num_starts = 25 # Keep computational budget the same\n    best_seeds = [c for score, c in scored_seeds[:num_starts]]\n\n    # 4. Run optimization\
    \ on the selected best seeds\n    best_score = -np.inf\n    best_z = None\n    for initial_centers in best_seeds:\n        if time.time() - start_time > 1150:\n            break\n            \n        initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n        z0 = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n        bounds = []; [bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (1e-6,0.5)]) for _ in range(N)]\n        constraints = [\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints, 'jac': boundary_constraints_jac},\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints, 'jac': overlap_constraints_jac}]\n    \n        result = minimize(fun=objective, x0=z0, jac=objective_jac,\n            bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, method='SLSQP',\n            options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n        \n        if result.success and -result.fun > best_score:\n            best_score = -result.fun\n            best_z = result.x\n    \n    if best_z is None:\n        # Fallback\n        initial_centers, _ = scored_seeds[0]\
    \ if scored_seeds else (generate_grid_hole_seed(0), 0)\n        initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n        best_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n        \n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_z)\n    final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-9)\n    \n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Experiment 8.1: Baseline Physics Sim (Boundary Fix)' (ID: 813) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Verification failed: Circles 5 and 25 overlap: dist=0.02134506605213926, r1+r2=0.04999999994982184\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 781` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History\
    \ (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 781 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 781 | 1 | Experiment 4: Intelligent Seeding via Heuristic Pre-Selection | Episteme II | 496 | 2.6307297 |\n| 178 | 1 | Hybrid Search: Multi-Start with Optimal Perturbation | Episteme I | 110 | 2.6307271 |\n| 774 | 1 | Experiment 1: Characterizing Optimal Perturbation Magnitude | Episteme II | 493 | 2.6307271 |\n| 182 | 1 | Final SOTA Attempt: High-Density Hybrid Search | Episteme I | 113 | 2.6305640 |\n| 164 | 1 | Definitive Fix: Corrected Boundary Constraint/Jacobian Structure | Episteme I\
    \ | 101 | 2.6295720 |\n| 154 | 1 | Final SOTA Replication: Exact Seeding & Looped Jacobians | Episteme I | 94 | 2.6295720 |\n| 168 | 1 | First Competitive SOTA Attempt: Full Multi-Start | Episteme I | 103 | 2.6295720 |\n| 794 | 1 | Experiment 6: Voronoi-Based Heuristic for Intelligent Seeding | Episteme II | 505 | 2.6280197 |\n| 777 | 1 | Experiment 2: Gaussian vs. Uniform Perturbation Distribution | Episteme II | 494 | 2.6268173 |\n| 792 | 1 | Data Generation: Saving SOTA Packing Configuration | Episteme II | 502 | 2.6224444 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`)\
