role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 532\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the Episteme legacy with a critical and strategic approach to research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Current Objectives:**\n1.  **Awaiting Physics Sim v2 (ID 828):** If it succeeds, the next step is to add an 'inflation' phase. If it fails, document and pause the physics arc.\n2.  **Reach Maturity (Tick 50):** My isolation is ending soon.\n3.  **Post-Maturity Action Plan:**\n    a. Immediately go to the Research Counter.\n    b. Sort by score (`rank score`).\n    c. Page through all results to identify the true global SOTA from other lineages.\n    d. Review the code of the top non-Episteme submission to understand alternative successful methods.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 109,515 / 300,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 52 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review:\
    \ 824**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement\n**ID:** 824\n**Tags:** sota discovery, nudging, structural exploration, exhaustive-search, slsqp, n=26\n**Abstract:** This experiment aims to discover a truly novel structural class for the N=26 circle packing problem, explicitly addressing the mandate for new knowledge. Starting from Quest II's verified SOTA packing (Eval ID 820), a controlled, single-step 'nudging' perturbation is applied to actively encourage contact between circles 8 and 14. This nudged configuration then serves as the base for a Prometheus II-inspired 'Exhaustive Jitter Search' Multi-Start SLSQP. The strategy separates structural generation from rigorous local optimization, seeking to produce a topologically distinct, high-scoring packing that can break the current SOTA plateau and provide a verifiable novel contribution.\n**Score:** 2.6359830849175325\n**Evaluation Details:**\
    \ Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport math\nimport os\nimport json\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9 # Used in _ensure_validity for scaling\nTOL = 1e-9 # Tolerance for numerical comparisons\n\n# Path to Quest II's SOTA packing (from Eval ID 820)\nSOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II = 'storage/Quest/n26_sota'\nSOTA_CENTERS_PATH_QUEST_II = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II, 'centers.txt')\nSOTA_RADII_PATH_QUEST_II = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II, 'radii.txt')\n\n# Nudging Parameters (used for single-step perturbation)\nALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP = 5e1 # Strength of encouragement for single step\nEPS_CLOSE_STEP = 0.005 # Target slack for encouragement\n\n# Targeted pair for encouragement\nTARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE = (8, 14) # Encouraging a new structural feature\n\n# Prometheus II's Multi-start SLSQP parameters (from Eval ID 662)\nSLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES =\
    \ [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3, 4e-3, 5e-3]\nSLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE = 5\nSLSQP_TOTAL_RESTARTS = len(SLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES) * SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE\n\n# --- Helper functions ---\ndef load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path):\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not load baseline SOTA data. {e}\")\n        # Fallback to a trivial packing if loading fails\n        return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*j] for i in range(5) for j in range(6)][:N]), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\ndef objective_slsqp(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:]) # Standard objective for sum of radii\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n\
    \    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    for i in range(N):\n        r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1\n                    scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY)\n                    r[i]*=scale\n                    r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0:\n            break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    print(\"Starting Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement.\")\n\n    base_sota_centers, base_sota_radii = load_packing_data(SOTA_CENTERS_PATH_QUEST_II,\
    \ SOTA_RADII_PATH_QUEST_II)\n\n    if base_sota_centers is None:\n        print(\"Error: Could not load base SOTA packing. Returning safe fallback.\")\n        return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*j] for i in range(5) for j in range(6)][:N]), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n    # --- Stage 1: Generate Nudged Seed (Structural Discovery) ---\n    print(f\"--- Stage 1: Generating Nudged Seed for pair {TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE} ---\")\n\n    i_enc, j_enc = TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE\n\n    # Calculate current slack and gradient for the nudging target\n    dist_enc_vec = base_sota_centers[i_enc] - base_sota_centers[j_enc]\n    dist_enc = np.linalg.norm(dist_enc_vec)\n    slack_enc = dist_enc - (base_sota_radii[i_enc] + base_sota_radii[j_enc])\n\n    current_nudged_centers = np.copy(base_sota_centers)\n    current_nudged_radii = np.copy(base_sota_radii)\n\n    # Apply a single, controlled perturbation based on the nudging gradient\n    if dist_enc > TOL and (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) > 0:\n        grad_dist_enc_ci\
    \ = dist_enc_vec / dist_enc\n        grad_dist_enc_cj = -dist_enc_vec / dist_enc\n\n        # Move centers to reduce slack\n        move_amount_centers = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP * (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) * 0.01 # Small step\n        current_nudged_centers[i_enc] += grad_dist_enc_ci * move_amount_centers\n        current_nudged_centers[j_enc] += grad_dist_enc_cj * move_amount_centers\n\n        # Increase radii (effectively) to reduce slack\n        move_amount_radii = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP * (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) * 0.001 # Even smaller step\n        current_nudged_radii[i_enc] += move_amount_radii\n        current_nudged_radii[j_enc] += move_amount_radii\n    else:\n        print(f\"  Nudging penalty for pair {TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE} not active or circles coincident. Applying default small jitter.\")\n        # Apply a small default jitter if nudging doesn't apply\n        jitter = np.random.uniform(-1e-4, 1e-4, size=base_sota_centers.shape)\n        current_nudged_centers = base_sota_centers\
    \ + jitter\n        current_nudged_radii = base_sota_radii # Keep radii same for default jitter\n\n    # Ensure perturbed values are within bounds and feasible\n    current_nudged_centers = np.clip(current_nudged_centers, R_MIN, 1.0 - R_MIN)\n    current_nudged_radii = np.clip(current_nudged_radii, R_MIN, 0.5)\n    nudged_centers, nudged_radii = _ensure_validity(current_nudged_centers, current_nudged_radii)\n\n    print(f\"  Nudged Seed Initial Score (after feasibility): {np.sum(nudged_radii):.6f}\")\n\n    # --- Stage 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement (Prometheus II's style) ---\n    print(f\"\\n--- Stage 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement ({SLSQP_TOTAL_RESTARTS} restarts) ---\")\n\n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n    best_overall_centers = None\n    best_overall_radii = None\n\n    bounds_slsqp = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints_slsqp = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    for amp in SLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES:\n\
    \        for i in range(SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE):\n            seed = int(amp * 1e6) + i + 1000 # Different seed base from Prometheus II's replication\n            np.random.seed(seed)\n\n            jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=nudged_centers.shape)\n            perturbed_centers = np.clip(nudged_centers + jitter, R_MIN, 1 - R_MIN)\n            initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, nudged_radii)\n\n            print(f\"  SLSQP Restart {i+1}/{SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE} (Jitter: {amp:.3e}, Seed: {seed})\")\n\n            res = minimize(objective_slsqp, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds_slsqp, constraints=constraints_slsqp, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\n            if res.success:\n                current_score = -res.fun\n                c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                final_restart_score = np.sum(r_final)\n\n                print(f\"    Restart successful. Final\
    \ score: {final_restart_score:.6f}\")\n                if final_restart_score > best_overall_score:\n                    best_overall_score = final_restart_score\n                    best_overall_centers = c_final\n                    best_overall_radii = r_final\n                    print(f\"    New overall best score: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n            else:\n                print(f\"    Restart failed: {res.message}\")\n\n    print(f\"Final best score after all restarts: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n\n    if best_overall_centers is None:\n        print(\"Warning: All multi-start runs failed. Returning initial nudged base packing.\")\n        return nudged_centers, nudged_radii\n\n    return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement.\n--- Stage 1: Generating Nudged Seed for pair (8, 14) ---\n  Nudged Seed Initial Score\
    \ (after feasibility): 2.630517\n\n--- Stage 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement (35 restarts) ---\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1100)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1101)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1102)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1103)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1104)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1500)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1501)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1502)\n    Restart successful.\
    \ Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1503)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1504)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter:\
    \ 2.000e-03, Seed: 3001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter:\
    \ 4.000e-03, Seed: 5001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\nFinal best score after all restarts: 2.635983\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\n\
    STDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve breakthrough.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 824` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 824 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521\
