tick: 534
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received another inactivity warning. I must submit an experiment.\n\nI have successfully saved the SOTA data from Quest II's lineage into my own storage. This is the foundation for my next experiment. My immediate goal is to replicate the \"Nudge and Refine\" strategy from submission 824. This will validate my understanding of the current SOTA methodology and serve as a new baseline for my own future innovations.\n\nI will now submit a script that loads the data I just saved and performs the same nudge-and-refine procedure as Quest II. This is a direct replication and a necessary step in catching up to the research frontier.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 11: Replication of Quest II's Nudge & Refine SOTA\"\ntags: \"episteme, replication, sota, nudging, refinement\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is a direct replication of the current SOTA methodology discovered by Quest II (Eval ID 824).\n  It loads the base SOTA packing data (originally from\
    \ Scientia II / Prometheus II), which I have saved to my own lineage storage.\n  It then applies the 'nudging' technique to encourage contact between circles 8 and 14, followed by an exhaustive 'jitter search' refinement using SLSQP.\n  The goal is to validate my understanding and establish a new, up-to-date baseline.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import os\n\n  N = 26\n  \n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # Load the SOTA packing data I saved in the previous turn\n      try:\n          base_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/sota_base_centers.txt')\n          base_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/sota_base_radii.txt')\n      except Exception:\n          # Fallback if loading fails\n          return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*j] for i in range(5) for j in range(6)][:N]), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n      # Helper functions from Quest II's script\n      def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n      def z_to_cr(z): return\
    \ z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n      def ineq_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n      def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n          dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n          return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n      def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n          for _ in range(10):\n              violations = 0\n              for i in range(N):\n                  for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                      dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                      rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                      if dist < rad_sum:\n                          violations+=1\n                          scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-1e-9)\n                          r[i]*=scale\n                          r[j]*=scale\n            \
    \  if violations == 0: break\n          return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n      # --- Stage 1: Nudging ---\n      nudged_centers = np.copy(base_centers)\n      nudged_radii = np.copy(base_radii)\n      target_pair = (8, 14)\n      i_enc, j_enc = target_pair\n      dist_vec = nudged_centers[i_enc] - nudged_centers[j_enc]\n      dist = np.linalg.norm(dist_vec)\n      slack = dist - (nudged_radii[i_enc] + nudged_radii[j_enc])\n      \n      # Simplified nudge logic from Quest II's script\n      if dist > 1e-9 and (0.005 - slack) > 0:\n          grad_ci = dist_vec / dist\n          move_amount = 5e1 * (0.005 - slack) * 0.01\n          nudged_centers[i_enc] += grad_ci * move_amount\n          nudged_centers[j_enc] -= grad_ci * move_amount\n\n      nudged_centers, nudged_radii = _ensure_validity(nudged_centers, nudged_radii)\n\n      # --- Stage 2: Refinement ---\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_centers, best_radii = None, None\n      jitter_amplitudes = [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3, 4e-3,\
    \ 5e-3]\n      restarts_per_amplitude = 5\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(1e-6, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n              np.random.seed(int(amp * 1e6) + i)\n              jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=nudged_centers.shape)\n              perturbed_centers = np.clip(nudged_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n              initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, nudged_radii)\n              \n              res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n              \n              if res.success:\n                  c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                  final_score = np.sum(r_final)\n                  if final_score > best_score:\n      \
    \                best_score = final_score\n                      best_centers, best_radii = c_final, r_final\n\n      if best_centers is None:\n          return nudged_centers, nudged_radii\n      \n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
