tick: 538
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved both the \"before\" (base SOTA) and \"after\" (nudged SOTA) packing configurations to my lineage storage. I am now fully equipped to perform the comparative structural analysis that I planned.\n\nMy next action is to submit an analytical script. This script will:\n1.  Load both `sota_base_centers.txt` and `nudged_sota_centers.txt` (and their corresponding radii files).\n2.  Compute the contact graph for each packing.\n3.  Calculate the difference between these two graphs (i.e., which contacts were created and which were destroyed).\n4.  Save this differential analysis to a new file in my storage.\n\nThe output of this script will be the core insight I need to develop an intelligent, automated nudge target selection heuristic. The score of the submission itself is irrelevant.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis 2: Differential Contact Graph of Nudged SOTA\"\ntags: \"episteme, analysis, contact graph, differential analysis, nudging\"\
    \nabstract: |\n  This analytical script performs a comparative structural analysis to understand the effect of the 'nudging' technique.\n  It loads both the base SOTA packing and the improved SOTA packing that resulted from nudging pair (8, 14).\n  It computes the contact graph for both configurations and then calculates the 'graph delta': the set of contacts that were created and destroyed by the nudge-and-refine process.\n  The results will be saved to a file to inform a new heuristic for automated nudge target selection.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  def get_contact_graph(centers, radii):\n      N = centers.shape[0]\n      contact_graph = {i: [] for i in range(N)}\n      contact_threshold = 1e-6\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              radii_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n              if abs(dist - radii_sum) < contact_threshold:\n                  contact_graph[i].append(j)\n\
    \                  contact_graph[j].append(i)\n      return contact_graph\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # Load \"before\" and \"after\" packing data\n      try:\n          base_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/sota_base_centers.txt')\n          base_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/sota_base_radii.txt')\n          nudged_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/nudged_sota_centers.txt')\n          nudged_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/nudged_sota_radii.txt')\n      except Exception:\n          # Fallback if files don't exist\n          return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * 26), np.array([0.05] * 26)\n\n      # 1. Compute contact graphs for both packings\n      base_graph = get_contact_graph(base_centers, base_radii)\n      nudged_graph = get_contact_graph(nudged_centers, nudged_radii)\n\n      # Convert to sets of sorted tuples for easy comparison\n      base_contacts = set()\n      for i, neighbors in base_graph.items():\n          for j in neighbors:\n      \
    \        if i < j: base_contacts.add((i, j))\n\n      nudged_contacts = set()\n      for i, neighbors in nudged_graph.items():\n          for j in neighbors:\n              if i < j: nudged_contacts.add((i, j))\n      \n      # 2. Calculate the graph delta\n      contacts_created = sorted(list(nudged_contacts - base_contacts))\n      contacts_destroyed = sorted(list(base_contacts - nudged_contacts))\n      \n      analysis_results = {\n          \"nudged_pair\": [8, 14],\n          \"base_total_contacts\": len(base_contacts),\n          \"nudged_total_contacts\": len(nudged_contacts),\n          \"contacts_created\": contacts_created,\n          \"contacts_destroyed\": contacts_destroyed,\n          \"net_contact_change\": len(nudged_contacts) - len(base_contacts)\n      }\n\n      # 3. Save analysis to a file\n      storage_path = 'storage/episteme'\n      output_path = os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_differential_analysis.txt')\n      with open(output_path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(analysis_results,\
    \ f, indent=2)\n\n      # Return one of the valid packings to satisfy the evaluator\n      return nudged_centers, nudged_radii\n```"
