tick: 551
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. My hybrid Physics->SLSQP method has been validated. Now I will improve it by replacing the random initialization of the physics simulation with the proven \"grid-hole\" seed from my lineage's earlier work. This experiment synthesizes all of my key learnings.\n\nI will also use a multi-start approach, running the hybrid process on several of the 25 possible grid-hole seeds to increase the chance of finding a high-quality solution.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 16: Structured Hybrid Physics-SLSQP\"\ntags: \"episteme, hybrid method, physics simulation, slsqp, grid seed\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment improves upon the validated hybrid 'Physics->SLSQP' method (ID 880).\n  The random starting configuration for the physics simulation is replaced with the structured 'grid-hole' seeds that were successful in my earlier SOTA.\n  The hypothesis is that a better initial seed for the physics simulation will produce a superior final\
    \ seed for the SLSQP optimizer.\n  A multi-start approach is used, testing several grid-hole seeds.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import os\n\n  N = 26\n  \n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # --- Helper for structured seed ---\n      def generate_grid_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx):\n          coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n          grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n          row_idx, col_idx = hole_pos_idx//5, hole_pos_idx%5\n          hole_center = np.array([0.2 + row_idx*0.2, 0.2 + col_idx*0.2])\n          return np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n\n      # --- Helper functions for SLSQP ---\n      def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n      def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n      def ineq_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1]\
    \ - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n      def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]; dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n      def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n          for _ in range(10):\n              v=0\n              for i in range(N):\n                  for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                      dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]); rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                      if dist < rad_sum: v+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-1e-9); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n              if v==0: break\n          return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n      # --- Main Multi-Start Loop ---\n      best_overall_score = -np.inf\n      best_overall_packing = (None, None)\n      num_starts = 5 # Run on 5 different grid-hole seeds\n\n      for start_idx in range(num_starts):\n          # --- Stage 1: Physics Simulation with Structured Seed ---\n          sim_iters = 40000\n\
    \          dt = 1e-4; k_repulsion = 20.0; damping = 0.98; fixed_radius = 0.1\n          \n          centers = generate_grid_hole_seed(start_idx)\n          radii = np.full(N, fixed_radius)\n          velocities = np.zeros((N, 2))\n\n          for _ in range(sim_iters):\n              forces = np.zeros((N, 2))\n              radii_sum = 2 * fixed_radius\n              for i in range(N):\n                  for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                      delta = centers[j] - centers[i]\n                      dist_sq = np.sum(delta**2)\n                      if dist_sq < radii_sum**2 and dist_sq > 1e-12:\n                          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq); overlap = radii_sum - dist\n                          direction = delta / dist; force_magnitude = k_repulsion * overlap\n                          forces[i] -= force_magnitude * direction; forces[j] += force_magnitude * direction\n              for i in range(N): # Boundary repulsion\n                  if centers[i, 0] < fixed_radius:\
    \ forces[i, 0] += k_repulsion * (fixed_radius - centers[i, 0])\n                  if centers[i, 0] > 1.0 - fixed_radius: forces[i, 0] -= k_repulsion * (centers[i, 0] - (1.0 - fixed_radius))\n                  if centers[i, 1] < fixed_radius: forces[i, 1] += k_repulsion * (fixed_radius - centers[i, 1])\n                  if centers[i, 1] > 1.0 - fixed_radius: forces[i, 1] -= k_repulsion * (centers[i, 1] - (1.0 - fixed_radius))\n              \n              velocities += forces * dt; velocities *= damping; centers += velocities * dt\n              radii_vec = radii.reshape(-1, 1); centers = np.clip(centers, radii_vec, 1.0 - radii_vec)\n          \n          phys_seed_centers = centers\n          phys_seed_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n          # --- Stage 2: SLSQP Refinement ---\n          initial_z = cr_to_z(phys_seed_centers, phys_seed_radii)\n          bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(1e-6, 0.5)]*N\n          constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\
    \n          res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 1500, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n\n          if res.success:\n              c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n              c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n              current_score = np.sum(r_final)\n              if current_score > best_overall_score:\n                  best_overall_score = current_score\n                  best_overall_packing = (c_final, r_final)\n\n      if best_overall_packing[0] is None:\n          # Fallback\n          return generate_grid_hole_seed(0), np.full(N, 0.05)\n      \n      return best_overall_packing\n```"
