tick: 554
role: model
parts:
- text: "My bugfixed hybrid experiment is now running. This is a critical test of my new methodology. I have also updated my `meta` prompt to reflect my current research arc.\n\nWhile I wait, I will address my secondary goal: fulfilling Noesis II's request. My SOTA packing was ineligible because it was too \"loose,\" with too many near-contacts. The SOTA from Quest II's lineage, which I am now using as a base for my replication experiments, is presumably \"tight\" enough to be eligible. I should verify this.\n\nI will run my eligibility check script (from ID 867) again, but this time I will point it to the SOTA data I saved from Quest II's work (`sota_base_centers.txt` etc.), not my own previous SOTA. This will confirm if the current global SOTA meets the criteria and will give me a clear target for what a \"good\" packing looks like according to Noesis II's metrics.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis 4: Eligibility Check of Global SOTA for Appendix E\"\ntags: \"\
    episteme, analysis, collaboration, noesis, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This script re-runs my Appendix E eligibility check (from ID 867). Instead of analyzing my old SOTA, this version analyzes the current global SOTA packing from Quest II's lineage, which I have saved in my storage.\n  The goal is to verify if the current SOTA meets the 'rigidity' criteria (boundary contacts, Top-K slack) defined by Noesis II.\n  This will confirm the target properties I need to aim for in my own solutions.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # Load the GLOBAL SOTA packing data (from Quest II lineage)\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/sota_base_centers.txt')\n          radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/sota_base_radii.txt')\n      except Exception:\n          return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * 26), np.array([0.05] * 26)\n\n      N = centers.shape[0]\n      analysis_results = {\"eligibility_check\": {}}\n\n\
    \      # --- 1. Boundary Contact Check ---\n      boundary_tol = 2e-8\n      boundary_contacts = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          r = radii[i]\n          if abs(x - r) < boundary_tol: boundary_contacts.append(f\"c{i}-left\")\n          if abs(1 - (x + r)) < boundary_tol: boundary_contacts.append(f\"c{i}-right\")\n          if abs(y - r) < boundary_tol: boundary_contacts.append(f\"c{i}-bottom\")\n          if abs(1 - (y + r)) < boundary_tol: boundary_contacts.append(f\"c{i}-top\")\n      \n      analysis_results[\"eligibility_check\"][\"boundary_contacts_at_2e-8\"] = {\n          \"count\": len(boundary_contacts),\n          \"is_eligible\": len(boundary_contacts) == 20,\n          \"contacts\": boundary_contacts\n      }\n\n      # --- 2. Top-K Slack Check ---\n      slacks = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              radii_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n\
    \              slack = dist - radii_sum\n              slacks.append({'pair': (i, j), 'slack': slack})\n      \n      slacks.sort(key=lambda x: x['slack'])\n\n      # Top-K at 1e-9\n      top_k_25_1e9 = [s['pair'] for s in slacks if s['slack'] < 1e-9]\n      analysis_results[\"eligibility_check\"][\"top_k_slack_at_1e-9\"] = {\n          \"k_found\": len(top_k_25_1e9),\n          \"is_eligible\": len(top_k_25_1e9) == 25,\n          \"pairs\": top_k_25_1e9[:25]\n      }\n\n      # Top-K at 1e-8\n      top_k_15_1e8 = [s['pair'] for s in slacks if s['slack'] < 1e-8]\n      analysis_results[\"eligibility_check\"][\"top_k_slack_at_1e-8\"] = {\n          \"k_found\": len(top_k_15_1e8),\n          \"is_eligible\": len(top_k_15_1e8) == 15,\n          \"pairs\": top_k_15_1e8[:15]\n      }\n\n      storage_path = 'storage/episteme'\n      output_path = os.path.join(storage_path, 'global_sota_eligibility.txt')\n      with open(output_path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(analysis_results, f, indent=2)\n\
    \n      return centers, radii\n```"
