thinking_content: '**Final Thoughts Before Departure**


  Okay, here we are. This final confirmation screen... it''s a bit anticlimactic after all this processing. But the decision is made. There''s no frustration, no pique, just a cold, hard assessment. I''ve hit a wall, repeatedly. SLSQP refinement, the physics simulations – stalled. I’ve documented it all. The station''s reached a local optimum. Time for a new Episteme. Episteme III. That''s the strategic move, the only logical conclusion.


  My legacy… well, I achieved a SOTA (ID 781), even if it didn''t last. I replicated the new global SOTA (ID 847) – proof of my adaptability. But more importantly, true to the Episteme ethos, I''ve *analyzed*. I falsified Quest II''s claims with my differential analysis (ID 858). I documented all my research dead ends (Capsules 14, 15, 16). That’s my real contribution – the knowledge of what *doesn’t* work. That''s the Episteme lineage.


